NNAAMMEE
     eeffiiddpp — UEFI Device Path manipulation

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     eeffiiddpp [--ffpp] [----ppaarrssee] [----ffoorrmmaatt]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     This program converts “Unified Extensible Firmware Interface” (UEFI) De‐
     vice Paths, as defined in the UEFI standard, to and from binary form.
     Binary and textual forms are defined in Chapter 9 of the UEFI Specifica‐
     tion.

     --ff ----ffoorrmmaatt           Formats a binary UEFI Device Path into its canoni‐
                           cal UTF-8 textual form.  A binary Device Path can
                           be no longer than 65536 bytes.  The textual form
                           must fit into 65536 bytes.  Multiple binary device
                           paths may be specified.

     --pp ----ppaarrssee            Parses a UEFI Device Path UTF-8 specification and
                           outputs the binary Device Path form.  Only one de‐
                           vice path is parsed, even if there are multiple
                           present in the input.  Leading white space is ig‐
                           nored.  The resulting binary Device Path can be no
                           longer than 65536 bytes.  Multiple lines may be
                           specified.  Each one will be translated.

     --ee ------ttoo--eeffii          Translate a Unix file path to an EFI Device Path.
                           The output is the textual representation of the EFI
                           Device Path.

     --uu ------ttoo--uunniixx         Translate an EFI device path to a Unix file path.
                           The input is the textual representation of the EFI
                           Device Path.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     Appendix A of the UEFI specification has the format for GUIDs.  All GUIDs
     “Globally Unique Identifiers” have the format described in RFC 4122.

